# Line endings — LF everywhere, including Windows checkouts.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# tools/meta_test.py mutates fomo_exit.py and restores it byte-for-byte (it has
# to: read_text/write_text once rewrote all 999 lines and left the file
# permanently "modified"). On a Windows checkout with autocrlf, git hands the
# harness a CRLF file, the harness faithfully writes CRLF back, and git then
# reports a 999-insertion/999-deletion diff with zero content change — every
# time preflight runs.
#
# Checking LF out on Windows makes the round-trip lossless. Python, Git Bash,
# and Railway (Linux) are all indifferent to which one is on disk.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the pieces where CRLF actively breaks something:
# a shell script with CRLF fails with a confusing "bad interpreter" error.
tools/hooks/* text eol=lf
*.sh         text eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary
*.docx binary
